-- Mount collection, same learn-once pattern as the companion pets
-- (20261004120000_world.sql, 20261005230630_world.sql). See /ARCHITECTURE.md.
--
-- Scope: every item_template row whose on-use spell applies
-- SPELL_AURA_MOUNTED (78), resolved through the server's own progressive
-- patch/build selection (item_template.patch against the live WowPatch=10,
-- spell_template.build against SUPPORTED_CLIENT_BUILD=5875), minus eleven
-- "Deprecated ..." placeholder rows the DB still carries (each superseded by
-- a real non-deprecated item at a different entry) and one GM-only test item
-- ("Foror's Fabled Steed") - neither obtainable by a real character.
--
-- Unlike the companion-pet migration, the new Summon spell for each mount is
-- a FULL clone of the original stock spell (every field, not a generic
-- template): mount speed (effectBasePoints2), level requirement (baseLevel),
-- duration and flavor text all carry real per-mount variation that a
-- template would have flattened. Only `entry` and `name` change.
-- equippedItemClass was already -1 on every one of the 107 unique mount
-- spells (verified programmatically before writing this, not assumed) - the
-- pilot's equip-requirement bug never applied to stock mount spells.
--
-- 107 new Summon spells and 112 new Teach spells (SPELL_EFFECT_LEARN_SPELL,
-- one per item - five items share a spell with another, same PvP-rank/
-- vendor-duplicate pattern as the companion pets' Moro'gai Gems, e.g. both
-- "Brown Horse Summoning" and PvP reward "Knight-Lieutenant's Steed" teach
-- the one shared Brown Horse). New reserved ID range 61000-61999, separate
-- from companion pets' 60000-60999 so the client can tell tabs apart by a
-- plain id-range check.
--
-- Four real name collisions in the source data (different spell ids
-- sharing a display name) resolved by hand: White Stallion/Black Ram/Ivory
-- Raptor each have a 60%-speed and a 100%-speed ("Swift ...") variant that
-- share one bare name in spell_template - prefixed the epic one "Swift ".
-- The two "Horn of the Red Wolf" items are a genuine data duplicate (same
-- creature, same speed, different allowable_race) - named "Red Wolf (Alt)"
-- rather than merged, since a player's race may only permit one of the two.
--
-- Teach spells carry spellVisual1=222, the same real "learned from a
-- trainer" visual the companion-pet Teach spells use (see
-- 20261005233000_world.sql) - not a separate choice, the same fix applies
-- here from the start.


DELETE FROM `item_template` WHERE (`entry`=875 AND `patch`=0)
   OR (`entry`=1041 AND `patch`=10)
   OR (`entry`=1132 AND `patch`=10)
